Good catch. This mirrors the same `str_replace('*/', ' ', ...)` trick PhpDumper already uses (PhpDumper.php:882) for the same problem, so it's not a new pattern here. But you're right it's lossier in this spot, since ArrayShapeGenerator is showing the actual default value to a reader, not mangling an internal doc block nobody reads literally. Splitting the star from the slash instead of collapsing both keeps it recognizable: `str_replace('*/', '* /', ...)` turns `*/30 * * * *` into `* /30 * * * *`, still safe but closer to the real value. Pushing that now.

